---
import InsertLayout from '../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Care Plans"
  description="One maintenance ladder for Toledo Technologies. Basic Care, Standard Support, Product Support, and Strategic Growth plans for websites, apps, and AI systems."
  heading="One maintenance ladder. Whatever we shipped, we maintain."
  subheading="Sites, web apps, mobile apps, SaaS systems, AI workflows — they all attach to the same plans. The thing you bought matters less than how alive it needs to be. Pick the level that matches the rhythm of your work."
>
  <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <span class="num">B6</span><span class="bar"></span><span>Care Plans</span>
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The two ladders</h2>
    <p>There are <strong>two ways</strong> to keep a system on retainer:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Care Plans</strong> — managed maintenance with monitoring, support,
        and care. Hours are part of the plan; the rest of the plan is the relationship.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Buckets</strong> — pure development hours, no monitoring, no support
        overhead. For clients who already know what they need built each month.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can move between them. Most clients start on a Care Plan after launch
      and graduate to a Bucket once they know their cadence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Care Plans</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 24px 0;">
        <thead>
          <tr
            style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gf-ink-200); text-align: left;"
          >
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Plan</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Monthly</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Hours included</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Best for</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Basic Care</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$750/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">2 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">Static or simple sites</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Standard Support</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$1,500/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">6 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">Active businesses, CMS-driven sites</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Product Support</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$4,500/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">15 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">Apps, SaaS, AI systems</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Strategic Growth</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$10,000+/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">40 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;"
              >Scaling startups, fractional engineering</td
            >
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>What's included at every tier</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Hours.</strong> Listed above. They cover bug fixes, content edits,
        small adjustments, security patches, and routine maintenance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monitoring.</strong> Uptime, performance, error tracking. We know
        before you do.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Response window.</strong> 1 business day on Basic Care; 4 hours on
        Standard; same-day on Product Support; 1 hour on Strategic Growth.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Front-of-queue priority.</strong> Retainer clients move ahead of project
        work for support requests.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Quarterly check-in.</strong> A short call covering performance, content,
        security, and what's next.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>Bucket Retainers (pure dev hours, no monitoring)</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 24px 0;">
        <thead>
          <tr
            style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gf-ink-200); text-align: left;"
          >
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Plan</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Monthly</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Hours</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Effective rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Starter Bucket</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$1,800/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">10 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$180/hr</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Growth Bucket</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$4,000/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">25 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$160/hr</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Scale Bucket</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$7,500/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">50 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$150/hr</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Buckets are for clients who already know what they need built each month
      and don't need monitoring on top.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>How to pick</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a website that mostly sits there — a Signal lander, an
      editorial site that updates a few times a quarter — <strong
        >Basic Care at $750/mo</strong
      > is enough. We patch security, fix bugs, swap content when you ask. Two hours
      covers it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your site or app is part of how the business operates — content goes
      out weekly, the contact form is a real lead source, the team makes edits,
      integrations sometimes wobble — <strong
        >Standard Support at $1,500/mo</strong
      > is the right level. Six hours is enough for the work; the monitoring is what
      catches the problems before customers do.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we shipped you a SaaS, an internal tool, a mobile app, or a production
      AI system, you almost certainly need <strong
        >Product Support at $4,500/mo or higher</strong
      >. Fifteen hours is the floor for systems that need active monitoring.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="inquire">
    <h2>Inquire about Care</h2>
    <form
      action="https://formsubmit.co/hello@toledotechnologies.com"
      method="POST"
      class="intake-form"
      style="display: grid; gap: 24px; max-width: 600px;"
    >
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New Care Plan Inquiry" />
      <input type="hidden" name="_honey" style="display:none" />

      <fieldset
        style="border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-200); padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px;"
      >
        <legend style="padding: 0 8px; font-weight: bold;"
          >About the system</legend
        >

        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          What kind of system needs care? *
          <select
            name="system_type"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          >
            <option value="">Select…</option>
            <option value="website"
              >Website (Signal / Editorial / Studio / Exodus / Atelier)</option
            >
            <option value="sitelift">SiteLift migrated site</option>
            <option value="web-app">Web app or internal tool</option>
            <option value="saas">SaaS product</option>
            <option value="mobile">Mobile app</option>
            <option value="ai">AI workflow / agent / production AI</option>
            <option value="multi">Multiple systems</option>
            <option value="other">Other</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          Did Toledo Technologies build it? *
          <select
            name="we_built_it"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          >
            <option value="">Select…</option>
            <option value="yes-recent">Yes — within the last year</option>
            <option value="yes-older">Yes — over a year ago</option>
            <option value="no-take-over"
              >No — looking for someone to take it over</option
            >
          </select>
        </label>

        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          Which plan are you considering? *
          <select
            name="plan_interest"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          >
            <option value="">Select…</option>
            <option value="basic-care">Basic Care ($750/mo)</option>
            <option value="standard-support"
              >Standard Support ($1,500/mo)</option
            >
            <option value="product-support">Product Support ($4,500/mo)</option>
            <option value="strategic-growth"
              >Strategic Growth ($10,000+/mo)</option
            >
            <option value="starter-bucket">Starter Bucket ($1,800/mo)</option>
            <option value="growth-bucket">Growth Bucket ($4,000/mo)</option>
            <option value="scale-bucket">Scale Bucket ($7,500/mo)</option>
            <option value="not-sure">Not sure — recommend</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          What's the work look like, in your own words?
          <textarea
            name="work_description"
            rows="5"
            placeholder="A few sentences. Frequency, system age, current pain, how alive it needs to be."
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          ></textarea>
        </label>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset
        style="border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-200); padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px;"
      >
        <legend style="padding: 0 8px; font-weight: bold;">Contact</legend>
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Name * <input
            type="text"
            name="name"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Email * <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Company <input
            type="text"
            name="company"
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
      </fieldset>

      <button
        type="submit"
        style="padding: 16px; background: var(--gf-ink-900); color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold;"
        >Submit inquiry — reply within 1 business day</button
      >

      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--gf-ink-500);">
        Care plans are quoted, not self-serve. We confirm fit, scope, and start
        date before invoicing. Full <a href="/terms">terms</a>.
      </p>
    </form>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section
    class="cta-banner"
    style="background: var(--gf-ink-900); color: white; padding: 48px; text-align: center;"
  >
    <p
      class="meta"
      style="text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"
    >
      B6 / Outro
    </p>
    <h2 style="font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
      Software that gets ignored fails quietly. Software that gets cared for
      compounds quietly.
    </h2>
    <p
      style="font-family: var(--gf-font-novel); font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 32px; opacity: 0.8;"
    >
      Pick the level that matches the rhythm of the work. We'll tell you if
      you've over-bought; we never under-quote.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/contact"
      style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; border: 1px solid white; color: white; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;"
      >Talk it through</a
    >
  </section>
</InsertLayout>
